  - id: CARD-228
    reason: "max_cycles 3 reached with the severity gate still open, min_improvement missed (8.0 -> 8.5 -> 8.0, needed >=9.0), and family regression for the THIRD consecutive cycle: each cycle's closed route reopens one syntactic level down - receiver, then binding form, then call shape and cross-call ink. Cycle 3 landed three more COMPLETE dot glyphs at 548 green: draw.line as a 240-ray fan (41x41 px, aspect 1.000, 1329 ink px against draw.ellipse's 1313 at the same radius - indistinguishable on a printed proof), a loop of in-bound draw.point calls (so the vertex bound is per-call and says nothing about ink accumulated across calls), and a stored bound method `stamp = draw.ellipse`."
    station: architect/owner
    route: "owner picks the instrument, then funds ONE cycle against it. (a) move `line` into the vertex-bounded set - BLOCKED, not merely expensive: two honest call sites (book_pdf_generator.py:1429 `ends`, :1441 `list(side)`; also png.py:186 and :217) are computed by construction and cannot pass a countable display, and this is the same regress the cycle-2 fix was right to refuse for receivers. (b) stop asking a syntax walk for a universal negative - switch AC-4's guard to render-and-measure: draw a page, find the ink, test it for roundness. The project already owns both halves (`_ink`/`_ink_box` live in this very test file), it is blind to spelling, all three cycle-3 survivors die instantly under it, and it is what CARD-207's printed proof does anyway. (c) narrow AC-4 to what is actually held, let the glyph land now, and card (b) as the follow-up the four adopting cards lean on. ORCHESTRATOR RECOMMENDATION: (c) then (b) - land the glyph, which is correct and verified, and fund the right instrument once as its own card rather than a fourth cycle here."
    at: 2026-10-16T19:45:00Z
    worktree_kept: ../PythonProject4-card-228
    branch: card/228-difficulty-dots
    head: 56cec05
    note: "The PRODUCT code is not in question: AC-1/2/3/5/6 green, geometry independently verified in cycles 1-2, the cycle-3 src delta is a single docstring hunk, G-5 holds with zero callers, G-1..G-5 hold, system contract 4 of 4, and both exemption sets rejected every absorption probe. What is unmet is AC-4 alone - a universal negative over Python syntax that four downstream cards were meant to lean on. Verified at this station before escalating: FLAT_METHODS' reason for leaving `line` unguarded is factually false. Pillow's own docstring reads 'Draw a line, or a connected sequence of line segments' and it calls draw_lines."
    resolved: "2026-10-16T19:55:00Z - owner chose option (c) then (b): AC-4 narrowed to the four routes a static walk can see, card returned to `review` for one bounded wording-and-limits pass, universal guarantee carded as CARD-241 (render-and-measure). Worktree was never discarded."
